          "Explanation: TS overloads consist of N call signatures followed by 1 implementation that must accept the union of all overload inputs.",
          "Q2: What is contextual typing?",
          "A) When TS infers parameter types from the expected type at the call site (*)",
          "B) When types are inferred from variable names",
          "C) When types are read from JSON files",
          "D) When types are generated by the OS",
          "Explanation: Contextual typing lets TS flow type information into expressions like callbacks where the expected type is known.",
          "Q3: What does `void` as a return type mean?",
          "A) The function must return undefined",
