          "Demonstrate a narrowing failure inside a `setTimeout` callback and fix it with a `const` capture.",
          "Use `in` to narrow a union `{ kind: \"a\"; a: number } | { kind: \"b\"; b: string }` based on which field exists.",
          "Combine `typeof` and `Array.isArray` to narrow `string | string[] | number` exhaustively.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 10) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: Which returns a boolean that narrows in the calling branch?",
          "A) `asserts x is T`",
          "B) `x is T` (user-defined type guard) (*)",
          "C) `as T`",
          "D) `<T>x`",
          "Explanation: A type guard (`x is T`) returns a boolean; the calling code's `if (isFoo(x))` branch narrows `x` to `Foo`.",
