          "A) https://example.com/page",
          "B) //example.com/page",
          "C) page.html (*)",
          "D) /page",
          "Explanation: `page.html` is relative to the current page's location; the others are absolute or protocol-relative.",
          "Q4: What is the purpose of `alt` on `<img>`?",
          "A) To provide alternative text for screen readers and failed loads (*)",
          "B) To show a tooltip",
          "C) To set the image size",
          "D) To cache the image",
          "Explanation: `alt` provides a text alternative read by screen readers and shown when the image cannot load.",
          "Q5: When should `alt=\"\"` (empty) be used?",
          "A) Never — it is invalid",
          "B) When the image is broken",
          "C) When the image is a link",
          "D) When the image is purely decorative (*)",
          "Explanation: Empty `alt` marks an image as decorative so screen readers skip it; never omit the attribute entirely.",
          "Q6: Which attributes prevent layout shift when an image loads?",
          "A) alt and title",
          "B) loading and decoding",
          "C) width and height (*)",
          "D) src and srcset",
          "Explanation: Specifying `width` and `height` lets the browser reserve space, preventing Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS).",
          "Q7: What does `loading=\"lazy\"` do on an `<img>`?",
          "A) Compresses the image",
          "B) Defers image load until it nears the viewport (*)",
          "C) Disables caching",
          "D) Forces synchronous loading",
          "Explanation: Native lazy loading defers offscreen images until the user scrolls near them, saving bandwidth and improving initial load.",
          "Q8: Which element wraps a captioned image?",
          "A) <caption>",
          "B) <legend>",
          "C) <aside>",
          "D) <figure> with <figcaption> (*)",
          "Explanation: `<figure>` groups media with its `<figcaption>` caption; `<caption>` is only for tables.",
          "Q9: What does `srcset` let the browser do?",
          "A) Validate HTML",
          "B) Preload the page",
          "C) Choose the best image source for the device (*)",
          "D) Add an alt text",
          "Explanation: `srcset` lists candidate images with descriptors (width or DPR); the browser selects the most appropriate one.",
