          "A) It is invalid HTML",
          "B) It breaks screen readers",
          "C) It disables the nav",
          "D) It is redundant; the role is implicit (*)",
          "Explanation: ARIA rule #1 says: don't add a role that duplicates native semantics. `<nav>` already implies `role=\"navigation\"`.",
          "Q5: Which element provides a machine-readable timestamp?",
          "A) <date>",
          "B) <timestamp>",
          "C) <meta name=\"date\">",
          "D) <time> with datetime attribute (*)",
          "Explanation: `<time datetime=\"2024-09-15\">` provides both a human-readable content and a machine-readable ISO timestamp.",
          "Q6: What is required inside a `<section>` element for valid semantics?",
          "A) A <p>",
          "B) An image",
          "C) A heading (h2-h6) (*)",
          "D) A list",
          "Explanation: `<section>` should always contain a heading; without one, use a `<div>` instead.",
