          "Q1: @SpringBootApplication combines?",
          "A) @Component, @Service, @Repository",
          "B) @Bean, @Autowired, @Component",
          "C) @Controller, @RestController, @RequestMapping",
          "D) @Configuration, @EnableAutoConfiguration, @ComponentScan (*)",
          "Explanation: @SpringBootApplication is a meta-annotation combining @Configuration (bean definitions), @EnableAutoConfiguration (auto-wiring), and @ComponentScan (component discovery).",
          "Q2: The recommended dependency injection style in Spring is?",
          "A) Constructor injection (*)",
          "B) Field injection (@Autowired on fields)",
          "C) Setter injection only",
          "D) Static injection",
          "Explanation: Constructor injection allows final fields, surfaces dependencies in the API, and is the Spring team's recommended approach. @Autowired on fields is discouraged.",
          "Q3: @RestController is shorthand for?",
          "A) @Controller + @Component",
          "B) @Controller + @ResponseBody (*)",
          "C) @Service + @RequestMapping",
          "D) @Configuration + @Bean",
          "Explanation: @RestController = @Controller + @ResponseBody (added at the type level). Every method's return value is serialized to the response body (typically JSON via Jackson).",
          "Q4: @WebMvcTest loads?",
          "A) The entire Spring context",
          "B) Only JPA repositories",
          "C) Only the web slice — controllers, converters, and MockMvc (*)",
          "D) Nothing — it's a no-op",
          "Explanation: @WebMvcTest loads only the web layer (controllers, MVC infra, MockMvc) — fast and isolated. Services are typically mocked with @MockBean.",
          "Q5: Bean Validation (@Valid, @NotBlank) integrates with Spring MVC by?",
          "A) Skipping validation",
          "B) Throwing SQLException",
          "C) Logging only",
          "D) Triggering MethodArgumentNotValidException on failure (*)",
          "Explanation: When @Valid fails, Spring throws MethodArgumentNotValidException, which a @ControllerAdvice can map to a 400 response with field-level error details.",
          "Q6: Spring Boot auto-configuration primarily relies on?",
          "A) @Conditional annotations (@ConditionalOnClass, @ConditionalOnMissingBean, etc.) (*)",
          "B) Reflection without conditions",
          "C) XML configuration files",
          "D) Manual bean wiring",
          "Explanation: Auto-configuration classes use @Conditional* annotations to register beans only when the classpath/properties are appropriate, enabling sensible defaults without manual wiring.",
          "Q7: @Transactional on a service method?",
          "A) Has no effect",
          "B) Wraps the method in a transaction; commits on normal return, rolls back on RuntimeException (*)",
          "C) Forces async execution",
          "D) Disables the persistence context",
          "Explanation: @Transactional (Spring's) opens a transaction, binds the EM to the thread, commits on normal return, and rolls back on unchecked exceptions by default.",
          "Q8: HikariCP is the default connection pool in Spring Boot because?",
          "A) It's the only pool that works",
          "B) Spring wrote it themselves",
          "C) It's fast, lightweight, and production-grade (*)",
          "D) It was the only choice pre-2015",
          "Explanation: HikariCP (~130KB) outperforms older pools (DBCP, c3p0, Tomcat JDBC) and has been the default since Spring Boot 2.0.",
