          "Send on a closed channel and observe the panic; then receive from a closed channel and observe ok=false.",
          "Build a select with two channels and observe the random selection over 100 iterations.",
          "Use a nil channel to dynamically enable/disable a select case.",
          "Trigger a `time.After` leak in a hot loop; profile with `pprof` and fix with `time.NewTimer`.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 11) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: What does sending on an unbuffered channel do?",
          "A) Returns immediately",
          "B) Panics",
          "C) Blocks until a receiver is ready (rendezvous) (*)",
          "D) Drops the value",
          "Explanation: Unbuffered channels are synchronous — the sender blocks until a receiver is ready to take the value, providing a rendezvous between goroutines.",
          "Q2: When does a buffered channel send block?",
          "A) Never",
          "B) Always",
          "C) Only when the buffer is empty",
          "D) Only when the buffer is full (*)",
          "Explanation: A buffered channel of capacity N accepts N sends without blocking; the (N+1)th send blocks until a receiver makes room.",
          "Q3: What happens when you send on a closed channel?",
          "A) Panics with \"send on closed channel\" (*)",
          "B) Returns an error",
          "C) Drops the value silently",
          "D) Reopens the channel",
          "Explanation: Sending on a closed channel panics. Only the sender should close, and only after all sends are done; receivers must never close.",
          "Q4: What does receiving from a closed channel return?",
