          "A) \"B\"",
          "B) \"A\" (*)",
          "C) Compile error",
          "D) Throws at runtime",
          "Explanation: Static dispatch uses the declared type `A`, so `A.f()` is called even though the runtime instance is `B`.",
          "Q9: Which stdlib API is implemented as extension functions?",
