          "Demonstrate that `ensure` runs even when `return` is called inside begin.",
          "Show that bare `rescue` catches StandardError but NOT a manually-raised Exception subclass.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 11) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: What does bare `rescue` (no class) catch?",
          "A) Exception only",
          "B) All errors including NoMemoryError",
          "C) StandardError only (NOT Exception) (*)",
          "D) Only RuntimeError",
          "Explanation: Bare rescue catches StandardError — rescuing Exception would trap Ctrl-C and out-of-memory errors.",
          "Q2: What does `raise` with no arguments do inside a rescue?",
          "A) Raises RuntimeError",
          "B) Returns nil",
          "C) Exits the program",
          "D) Re-raises the current exception (*)",
          "Explanation: Bare raise in a rescue re-raises the in-flight exception — useful after logging.",
          "Q3: When does `ensure` execute?",
          "A) Always — even on exception or explicit return (*)",
          "B) Only on exception",
          "C) Only on success",
          "D) Only when re-raising",
          "Explanation: ensure runs no matter how the begin block exits — perfect for cleanup.",
          "Q4: Where is `retry` valid?",
          "A) Anywhere in a method",
          "B) Only inside a rescue block (*)",
          "C) Inside ensure",
          "D) Inside else",
          "Explanation: retry re-runs the begin block from the top; only legal inside rescue.",
