          "A) Slower than rescue StandardError",
          "B) Doesn't catch anything",
          "C) Causes syntax errors",
          "D) Traps Ctrl-C, NoMemoryError, and SignalException (*)",
          "Explanation: Exception is the root — rescuing it traps system-level signals you usually want to let propagate.",
          "Q7: What does `expr rescue default` (modifier form) do?",
          "A) Returns default if expr raises StandardError (*)",
          "B) Returns default if expr returns nil",
          "C) Raises default",
          "D) Skips default",
          "Explanation: Modifier rescue catches StandardError and returns the fallback value; useful for one-liners like `Integer(s) rescue 0`.",
