          "Q6: What does roxygen2 generate when you run devtools::document()?",
          "A) man/*.Rd documentation files and NAMESPACE (*)",
          "B) The R/ source files",
          "C) The tests/ folder",
          "D) The DESCRIPTION file",
          "Explanation: roxygen2 parses #' comments above functions and generates man/*.Rd docs and NAMESPACE (if @export is present); DESCRIPTION is hand-edited (with usethis::use_package() helpers).",
          "Q7: What does @export in a roxygen comment do?",
          "A) Removes the function from the package",
          "B) Adds the function to NAMESPACE so users can call it directly (*)",
          "C) Hides the function",
          "D) Runs the function on package load",
          "Explanation: @export adds the function to NAMESPACE, making it accessible as pkg::fun() or fun() after library(pkg); internal helpers omit @export.",
          "Q8: What is the goal of R CMD check before CRAN submission?",
          "A) 0 errors only",
          "B) Passing tests only",
          "C) 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes (*)",
          "D) Documented functions",
          "Explanation: CRAN requires 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes; even minor notes (e.g. 'NOTE: no visible binding for global variable') cause rejection. Use devtools::check() locally and on CI.",
