          "B) `class X { static X get i => X(); }`",
          "C) `class X { static final X i = X._(); X._(); factory X() => i; }` (*)",
          "D) `class X { X() {} }`",
          "Explanation: Private constructor + static final instance + factory that returns the instance is the canonical Dart singleton pattern.",
          "Q6: What is `Object.hash(a, b, c)` used for?",
          "A) Computing a cryptographic hash",
          "B) Comparing two objects for equality",
          "C) Hashing strings for storage",
          "D) Implementing hashCode by combining field hashes (*)",
          "Explanation: `Object.hash(...)` combines multiple field hashes into a single int using a mixing function; it's the recommended `hashCode` implementation.",
          "Q7: If you define a named constructor `Point.origin()`, what happens to the default `Point()`?",
          "A) It remains available alongside any named constructor (*)",
          "B) It still exists",
          "C) It still exists only if you don't define any other constructor",
          "D) It disappears only if you also define a default — otherwise it's still there",
          "Explanation: Defining a named constructor does NOT remove the default; only defining a generative (default-replacement) constructor does. Both can coexist.",
          "Q8: What happens if you mutate a field used as a Map key after insertion?",
          "A) Map updates automatically",
          "B) The entry becomes unreachable — broken lookup (*)",
          "C) Map throws",
          "D) Nothing — fields are always immutable",
          "Explanation: Hash-based collections bucket by the key's hash at insertion; mutating the key changes its hash but not its bucket, so lookups fail silently.",
