          "A) Point(x) — assigns the param to the field x",
          "B) Point(x = this.x)",
          "C) Point(this.x) — assigns the param to the field x (*)",
          "D) Point(x: this)",
          "Explanation: `Point(this.x)` is sugar for `Point(x) : this.x = x;` — the parameter name matches the field and is auto-assigned via the initializer list.",
          "Q10: What does `late final` enable?",
          "A) A mutable field that can be reassigned",
          "B) A field that is always null initially",
          "C) A field that is thread-safe",
          "D) A const-like field that is set once at runtime, possibly lazily (*)",
          "Explanation: `late final` allows a field to be assigned exactly once at runtime (often lazily via inline initializer), useful when construction-time init isn't possible.",
