          "Send a 10MB `Uint8List` between isolates; measure the time.",
          "Use `TransferableTypedData` to send the same buffer and compare timings.",
          "Trigger `compute` from a Flutter app for a slow sort and observe UI smoothness.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 15) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: What is an isolate?",
          "A) A thread with shared memory",
          "B) A deprecated async primitive",
          "C) A worker with its own heap and event loop (*)",
          "D) A type of Future",
          "Explanation: Isolates are Dart's unit of concurrency; each has independent memory and an event loop, communicating only by message passing.",
          "Q2: How do isolates share data?",
          "A) Shared globals",
          "B) Mutex-protected fields",
          "C) They can't communicate",
          "D) Message passing (no shared memory) (*)",
          "Explanation: Isolates have separate heaps; the only way to share data is to send a copy via SendPort/ReceivePort. No shared mutable state.",
          "Q3: What does `Isolate.run(fn)` do?",
          "A) Spawns an isolate, runs fn, returns the result, tears down (*)",
          "B) Runs fn on the current isolate",
          "C) Spawns a long-lived isolate",
          "D) Cancels the current isolate",
          "Explanation: `Isolate.run` is the one-shot API: spawn, compute, return result, dispose. Ideal for parallel CPU-bound chunks.",
