          "A) It's required by Docker",
          "B) It replaces the entrypoint shell with the main command (PID 1) so signals reach it directly (*)",
          "C) It makes the script faster",
          "D) It backgrounds the command",
          "Explanation: Without exec, the main command would run as a child of the shell, and signals like SIGTERM wouldn't propagate cleanly. exec makes the command PID 1.",
          "Q10: How do you mitigate a fork bomb?",
          "A) Reboot every minute",
          "B) Disable bash",
          "C) Use `ulimit -u N` to cap per-user process count; logrotate processes; cgroups (*)",
          "D) Remove the function keyword",
