          "Explanation: A single-line `'use client'` directive at the very top of a file marks it (and its imports) as client-bundled, enabling hooks, events, and browser APIs.",
          "Q2: Which of these can a Server Component do that a Client Component cannot?",
          "A) Use useState",
          "B) Read from a database directly (*)",
          "C) Add event handlers",
          "D) Render JSX",
          "Explanation: Server components can import database clients, fs, and process.env secrets because they never ship to the browser; client components cannot do these without leaking secrets.",
          "Q3: What happens if you try to pass a function as a prop from a server to a client component?",
          "A) It works fine",
          "B) It silently fails",
          "C) The build fails because functions are not serializable across the RSC boundary (*)",
          "D) The function runs on the server",
          "Explanation: The RSC protocol serializes props as JSON; functions cannot cross the boundary, so the build fails. Use Server Actions or define the handler client-side.",
          "Q4: What does the `server-only` package do?",
          "A) Marks a component as server-rendered only (no client prerender)",
          "B) Optimizes server bundle size",
