          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 7) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: What method must you call in URLconf to use a CBV?",
          "A) .view()",
          "B) .render()",
          "C) .as_view() (*)",
          "D) .dispatch()",
          "Explanation: CBVs are classes; .as_view() returns a callable that Django can invoke with a request. The callable creates an instance and calls dispatch().",
          "Q2: Which method on a ListView should you override to filter the queryset?",
          "A) get()",
          "B) get_object()",
          "C) filter()",
          "D) get_queryset() (*)",
          "Explanation: get_queryset returns the queryset used for both list rendering and pagination count. Overriding get() bypasses pagination.",
          "Q3: In what order should mixins be listed?",
          "A) LoginRequiredMixin leftmost, then other mixins, then the view class (*)",
          "B) Alphabetically",
          "C) View class first, mixins last",
          "D) Doesn't matter",
          "Explanation: LoginRequiredMixin.dispatch must run first to gate access. Mixins precede the main view class so their methods can override.",
          "Q4: Which method handles a successful form submission in CreateView?",
          "A) form_invalid()",
          "B) form_valid() (*)",
          "C) save()",
          "D) success()",
          "Explanation: form_valid(form) saves the form, sets self.object, and returns a redirect to get_success_url(). Override to inject extra logic.",
          "Q5: How do you add a template variable in a CBV?",
          "A) Override get_template()",
          "B) Set self.context",
          "C) Override get_context_data() and add to the dict (*)",
          "D) Pass it in as_view()",
          "Explanation: get_context_data(**kwargs) returns the template context. Always call super() first and merge.",
          "Q6: Which CBV displays a single object by pk or slug?",
          "A) ListView",
          "B) SingleView",
          "C) ShowView",
          "D) DetailView (*)",
          "Explanation: DetailView fetches one object via get_object_or_404 using pk_url_kwarg or slug_url_kwarg from the URL.",
          "Q7: What's the correct way to set the redirect target after a CreateView save?",
          "A) Override get_success_url() or set success_url (*)",
          "B) Set self.redirect",
          "C) Return a string from form_valid",
          "D) Use redirect_to attribute",
          "Explanation: get_success_url() is called by form_valid; you can set success_url = \"/\" or override the method for dynamic URLs (e.g., return self.object.get_absolute_url()).",
          "Q8: What does UserPassesTestMixin require you to implement?",
          "A) check_user()",
          "B) test_func() returning a bool (*)",
          "C) has_permission()",
          "D) permission_required",
          "Explanation: test_func(self) returns True/False; False -> 403 (or redirect to login if raise_exception=False). Used for object-level checks.",
          "Q9: What does self.kwargs contain in a CBV?",
          "A) The model's kwargs",
          "B) The form's kwargs",
          "C) URL keyword arguments captured by path converters (*)",
          "D) Settings overrides",
          "Explanation: For path(\"post/<int:pk>/\"), self.kwargs == {\"pk\": 42}. Use it in get_object/get_queryset to filter.",
          "Q10: Why is overriding get() in a ListView usually wrong?",
          "A) get() doesn't exist in ListView",
          "B) It triggers an extra query",
          "C) It conflicts with as_view()",
          "D) It bypasses pagination and context setup that the BaseListView's get provides (*)",
          "Explanation: ListView's get() calls get_queryset(), paginates, and renders. Bypassing it with a custom get() means re-implementing all of that — prefer get_queryset or get_context_data.",
          "----------------------------------------------------------------------"
