          "A) Use @pytest.mark.asyncio",
          "B) Skip those tests",
          "C) Mock transaction.on_commit",
          "D) Use captureOnCommitCallbacks or pytest-django-pg (transaction=True) (*)",
          "Explanation: on_commit callbacks don't fire in a savepoint test. Use django.test.utils.captureOnCommitCallbacks or run the test with transaction=True.",
          "Q9: Why use reverse() in tests instead of hard-coded URLs?",
          "A) URL refactors don't break tests; tests stay decoupled from URL strings (*)",
          "B) It's faster",
          "C) reverse() is required by DRF",
          "D) It triggers middleware",
          "Explanation: reverse(\"post-list\") resolves to the URL at test time. If you change URLs, the test still works.",
          "Q10: What's a good branch coverage floor for a Django project?",
