          "Q4: How do you mark a query param as deprecated in /docs?",
          "A) Prefix the name with `deprecated_`",
          "B) Pass `deprecated=True` to `Query()` (*)",
          "C) Add `@deprecated` from typing",
          "D) You can't — deprecation is OpenAPI-only",
          "Explanation: `Query(deprecated=True)` flags the param in the OpenAPI schema, and Swagger UI shows it struck-through.",
          "Q5: What is `alias` used for in `Query(alias=\"t\")`?",
          "A) To rename the Python variable internally",
          "B) To forward the request to another route",
          "C) To expose a different key in the URL/JSON than the Python attribute name (*)",
          "D) To log the param under a different name",
          "Explanation: `alias` maps an external key (e.g., a short URL param) to a Python-safe attribute name.",
          "Q6: What happens if you send a JSON body to a GET route?",
          "A) FastAPI always rejects it with 415",
          "B) It works reliably everywhere",
          "C) FastAPI converts it to query params",
          "D) Many clients/proxies strip GET bodies; design GETs to use query params (*)",
          "Explanation: HTTP allows GET bodies but they're rarely honored end-to-end; use POST for bodies, GET for query params.",
          "Q7: How many body models can one route declare?",
          "A) Multiple — FastAPI wraps them in a JSON object keyed by param name (*)",
          "B) Exactly one",
          "C) Zero or one",
