          "C) Field-level defaults",
          "D) Strict integer parsing",
          "Explanation: It allows `Model.model_validate(orm_obj)` to read attributes off any object, not just dicts — essential for SQLAlchemy ORM rows.",
          "Q4: What does `extra=\"forbid\"` do on a Pydantic model?",
          "A) Forbids private attributes",
          "B) Forbids computed fields",
          "C) Forbids all extra fields, returning 422 on unknown keys (*)",
          "D) Forbids inheritance",
          "Explanation: With `extra=\"forbid\"` (set via `ConfigDict`), unknown fields in the incoming JSON raise a validation error.",
          "Q5: Which mode runs a validator before Pydantic's type coercion?",
          "A) `mode=\"after\"`",
          "B) `mode=\"raw\"`",
          "C) `mode=\"strict\"`",
          "D) `mode=\"before\"` (*)",
          "Explanation: `mode=\"before\"` receives the raw input (often a string or dict); `mode=\"after\"` receives the coerced value.",
          "Q6: How do you validate a value that depends on multiple fields?",
          "A) Use `@model_validator(mode=\"after\")` (*)",
          "B) Use two `@field_validator`s",
          "C) Use a custom `__init__`",
          "D) Use `Field(validator=...)`",
          "Explanation: `@model_validator(mode=\"after\")` has access to the fully-constructed `self` and can compare fields.",
          "Q7: Which is required on `@field_validator` in Pydantic v2?",
