      {
        "kind": "miniProject",
        "content": "Build a \"Production-Ready Middleware Stack\": Add CORS (one explicit origin), GZip (min 1KB), TrustedHost, request-id, and timing middleware to a small FastAPI app. Verify response headers include `X-Request-ID` and `X-Elapsed-Ms`. Confirm `/health` is fast. Suggested approach:\n  - Add `CORSMiddleware` with `allow_origins=[\"https://app.example.com\"]`\n  - Add `GZipMiddleware(minimum_size=1000)`\n  - Add `TrustedHostMiddleware(allowed_hosts=[\"api.example.com\"])`\n  - Write `@app.middleware(\"http\")` setting `request.state.request_id`\n  - Return headers on the response; test with `curl -i -H \"Origin: https://app.example.com\"`"
      },
      {
        "kind": "exercises",
        "items": [
          "Add `CORSMiddleware` and test from a browser-based fetch (or `curl -H \"Origin: ...\"`) to verify `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`.",
          "Add a request-id middleware that sets `request.state.request_id` and reads it in a route.",
          "Add GZipMiddleware and confirm large JSON responses get `Content-Encoding: gzip`.",
          "Write a pure ASGI middleware that adds a header and verify ordering vs `@app.middleware(\"http\")`.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 11) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: What's the execution order of middleware?",
          "A) First-added runs first on request",
          "B) Alphabetical by name",
          "C) Last-added runs first on request, last on response (*)",
          "D) Random",
          "Explanation: Middleware wraps the app like layers of an onion; the outermost (last added) is the first to see the request and the last to see the response.",
          "Q2: What happens if you set `allow_origins=[\"*\"]` with `allow_credentials=True`?",
          "A) It works fine",
          "B) Only GET is allowed",
          "C) Cookies are auto-attached",
          "D) Browsers reject the combination (*)",
          "Explanation: The CORS spec forbids wildcard origins with credentials; you must list explicit origins when cookies are involved.",
          "Q3: Which handles the CORS preflight (`OPTIONS`) request?",
          "A) CORSMiddleware (automatically) (*)",
          "B) The route handler",
          "C) GZipMiddleware",
          "D) The ASGI server",
          "Explanation: `CORSMiddleware` intercepts `OPTIONS` preflight and returns the appropriate `Access-Control-Allow-*` headers.",
          "Q4: Which is faster: `@app.middleware(\"http\")` or a pure ASGI middleware?",
          "A) `@app.middleware(\"http\")`",
          "B) Pure ASGI middleware (*)",
          "C) They're identical",
          "D) Depends on Python version",
          "Explanation: `@app.middleware(\"http\")` uses `BaseHTTPMiddleware` which adds overhead; pure ASGI middleware skips the request/response wrapping.",
          "Q5: What is `request.state` for?",
          "A) Caching across requests",
          "B) Storing sessions",
          "C) Stashing per-request data (e.g., request_id) (*)",
          "D) Holding global config",
          "Explanation: `request.state` is a per-request namespace; middleware can write to it and handlers can read from it.",
          "Q6: Why must `/health` be fast?",
          "A) It's a special route",
          "B) It doesn't run middleware",
          "C) It can't return JSON",
          "D) Load balancers probe it frequently; slow responses cause deregistration (*)",
          "Explanation: LBs probe health endpoints every few seconds; if middleware makes them slow, the LB may consider the instance unhealthy.",
          "Q7: Which middleware redirects HTTP to HTTPS?",
          "A) `HTTPSRedirectMiddleware` (*)",
          "B) `CORSMiddleware`",
          "C) `TrustedHostMiddleware`",
          "D) `GZipMiddleware`",
          "Explanation: `HTTPSRedirectMiddleware` returns a 307 redirect to the HTTPS URL.",
          "Q8: What does `GZipMiddleware(minimum_size=1000)` do?",
          "A) Compresses all responses",
          "B) Compresses responses larger than 1000 bytes (*)",
          "C) Limits response size to 1000 bytes",
          "D) Decompresses request bodies",
          "Explanation: Only responses above `minimum_size` are gzipped (small ones aren't worth the overhead).",
          "Q9: Why avoid blocking I/O in middleware?",
          "A) Middleware can't use I/O",
          "B) Blocking I/O is insecure",
          "C) It stalls the event loop for every request (*)",
          "D) It causes CORS errors",
          "Explanation: Middleware runs on the event loop; blocking I/O stalls every concurrent request on the worker.",
          "Q10: How do you add a custom ASGI middleware class?",
          "A) `@app.middleware(\"asgi\")`",
          "B) `app.middleware.append(MyMiddleware)`",
          "C) `MyMiddleware.register(app)`",
          "D) `app.add_middleware(MyMiddleware)` (*)",
          "Explanation: `app.add_middleware(cls, **kwargs)` instantiates the class wrapping the app; the class must accept `app` in `__init__`.",
          "----------------------------------------------------------------------"
        ]
      }
