          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 8) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: Which is the shorthand for v-on:click?",
          "A) :click",
          "B) #click",
          "C) ->click",
          "D) @click (*)",
          "Explanation: `@click` is the shorthand for `v-on:click`; `:` is for v-bind and `#` is for v-slot.",
          "Q2: What's the difference between @click=\"handler\" and @click=\"handler()\"?",
          "A) The first passes the event automatically; the second is an inline call where you pass $event explicitly (*)",
          "B) No difference",
          "C) The first is invalid",
          "D) The second is invalid",
          "Explanation: A method handler `@click=\"handler\"` receives the event as the first argument; an inline call `@click=\"handler()\"` runs the function and uses `$event` for the event.",
          "Q3: What does @click.stop do?",
          "A) Calls event.preventDefault()",
          "B) Calls event.stopPropagation() (*)",
          "C) Runs the handler only once",
          "D) Cancels the click",
          "Explanation: `.stop` calls `event.stopPropagation()` so the event does not bubble to ancestors.",
          "Q4: What does @submit.prevent do?",
          "A) Stops propagation",
          "B) Disables the submit button",
          "C) Calls event.preventDefault() to stop the form from submitting (*)",
          "D) Validates the form",
          "Explanation: `.prevent` calls `event.preventDefault()`, preventing the default form submission and page reload.",
          "Q5: What does .passive signal to the browser?",
          "A) The handler is async",
          "B) The handler runs only once",
          "C) The handler runs on a Web Worker",
          "D) The handler will never call preventDefault, enabling scroll perf optimizations (*)",
          "Explanation: `.passive` is a hint that the handler will not cancel the event, letting the browser optimize scrolling and touch.",
