          "B) Cancels the navigation silently (*)",
          "C) Throws an error",
          "D) Reloads the page",
          "Explanation: Returning `false` from a guard cancels the navigation; returning a route location object redirects to that route.",
          "Q5: How do you lazy-load a route component?",
          "A) component: lazy(\"./X.vue\")",
          "B) lazy: true",
          "C) component: () => import(\"./X.vue\") (*)",
          "D) async: true",
          "Explanation: A dynamic import `() => import(\"./X.vue\")` lets the bundler code-split the route component into a separate chunk loaded on navigation.",
          "Q6: Which hook runs before every navigation?",
          "A) router.beforeAll",
          "B) router.onEach",
          "C) router.pre",
          "D) router.beforeEach (*)",
          "Explanation: `router.beforeEach((to, from) => ...)` runs before every navigation globally; per-route guards use `beforeEnter`.",
          "Q7: What's required on the server when using createWebHistory?",
          "A) A fallback to index.html for unknown paths (*)",
          "B) Nothing",
          "C) A CDN",
          "D) HTTPS",
