          "Q1: Which module is required for `[(ngModel)]` and template-driven forms?",
          "A) ReactiveFormsModule",
          "B) FormsModule (*)",
          "C) CommonModule",
          "D) HttpClientModule",
          "Explanation: `FormsModule` provides `ngModel` and template-driven form directives; standalone components must add it to `imports: [...]`.",
          "Q2: Which module provides `FormControl`, `FormGroup`, and `FormBuilder`?",
          "A) FormsModule",
          "B) FormsCore",
          "C) ReactiveFormsModule (*)",
          "D) NgModelModule",
          "Explanation: `ReactiveFormsModule` exports the reactive forms APIs — FormControl, FormGroup, FormArray, FormBuilder, and the `formControlName` directive.",
          "Q3: What does `FormBuilder.nonNullable.group({...})` produce?",
          "A) A form whose values are always null",
          "B) A form without validators",
          "C) A form with no submit handler",
          "D) A typed form where empty fields default to '' instead of null (*)",
          "Explanation: `nonNullable` makes controls non-nullable — empty fields stay `''` (or `0` for numbers), and `form.value` is typed as non-nullable throughout.",
          "Q4: Which form type builds the model asynchronously from the template?",
          "A) Template-driven forms (*)",
          "B) Reactive forms",
          "C) Both",
          "D) Neither",
          "Explanation: Template-driven forms create the model after the view initializes (async); reactive forms declare the model first (sync) and bind it to the view.",
