          "Add multi-slot projection with `[card-title]` and `[card-actions]` selectors.",
          "Use `viewChild` to access a child component and call one of its methods from a button.",
          "Use `contentChild.required<TemplateRef<unknown>>('tpl')` to read a projected template and render it via `ngTemplateOutlet`.",
          "Convert a legacy `@ViewChild` decorator query to a signal `viewChild()` and use it in an `effect`.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 14) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: Which tag enables content projection in Angular?",
          "A) <slot>",
          "B) <ng-content> (*)",
          "C) <project>",
          "D) <inject>",
          "Explanation: `<ng-content>` marks where projected content is rendered; `<slot>` is the Web Components equivalent Angular does not use directly.",
          "Q2: Which attribute on `<ng-content>` enables multi-slot projection?",
          "A) slot",
          "B) name",
          "C) select (*)",
          "D) target",
          "Explanation: `select=\"...\"` accepts a CSS-like selector (element, [attribute], .class) to match specific projected content for that slot.",
          "Q3: Which signal-based API queries elements in a component's OWN view?",
          "A) contentChild()",
          "B) childQuery()",
          "C) queryChild()",
          "D) viewChild() (*)",
          "Explanation: `viewChild()` queries the component's own template; `contentChild()` queries content projected via `<ng-content>`.",
          "Q4: When is `@ContentChild` first available?",
          "A) In ngAfterContentInit (*)",
          "B) In the constructor",
          "C) In ngOnInit",
          "D) In ngAfterViewInit",
          "Explanation: Projected content is resolved before view init; access via `ngAfterContentInit` (decorator) or read reactively in an `effect()` for signal queries.",
          "Q5: What does `contentChild.required<T>()` do if no matching content is projected?",
          "A) Returns undefined",
          "B) Throws NG0950 (*)",
          "C) Returns null",
          "D) Renders an empty string",
          "Explanation: The `.required` variant throws NG0950 when no matching content is projected; use the non-required variant for optional content.",
          "Q6: Which directive renders a `TemplateRef` at a location with an optional context?",
          "A) [ngTemplateOutlet]",
          "B) ngProjectAs",
          "C) ngTemplate (*)",
          "D) ngContent",
          "Explanation: `<ng-container [ngTemplateOutlet]=\"tpl\" [ngTemplateOutletContext]=\"ctx\">` renders a `TemplateRef` with optional `$implicit` and named context values.",
