          "Q9: What happens if a secondary falls behind the oplog's oldest entry?",
          "A) It catches up automatically",
          "B) It becomes the primary",
          "C) Nothing changes",
          "D) It must do a full initial sync (resync from scratch) (*)",
          "Explanation: If the secondary can't find the next oplog entry (it's been overwritten), it can't catch up incrementally — it must do a full initial sync.",
