          "Create a capped collection (10MB, max 100k docs), insert 5 docs, and confirm `$natural` ordering.",
          "Open a tailable cursor on the capped collection in Node and insert a doc from another shell; confirm the cursor emits it.",
          ">>> QUIZ (Stage 19) <<<",
          "(Z AI: render this as an interactive multiple-choice quiz in the Learn tab)",
          "Q1: What is a time series collection optimized for?",
          "A) Frequent updates to existing documents",
          "B) Relational joins",
          "C) Append-only timestamped measurements with fast time-range queries (*)",
          "D) Full-text search",
          "Explanation: Time series collections use columnar-like compression and time-ordered storage to optimize append-only telemetry; updates/deletes are limited.",
