          "A) metaField",
          "B) granularity",
          "C) expireAfterSeconds",
          "D) timeField (*)",
          "Explanation: `timeField` (the timestamp) is required and indexed; `metaField` and `granularity` are optional (but recommended).",
          "Q3: What does a capped collection do when it's full?",
          "A) Silently overwrites the OLDEST documents (*)",
          "B) Stops accepting writes",
          "C) Errors out",
          "D) Auto-scales",
          "Explanation: Capped collections are fixed-size and FIFO — when full, new inserts overwrite the oldest documents, so head-of-line data is lost if the consumer is slow.",
          "Q4: Which cursor type lets you `tail -f` new inserts on a capped collection?",
          "A) change stream",
