          "D) covered cursor",
          "Explanation: `find().addCursorFlag(\"tailable\", true).addCursorFlag(\"awaitData\", true)` keeps the cursor open and blocks for new inserts — `tail -f` style. Only works on capped collections.",
          "Q5: What's a pitfall of `granularity: \"seconds\"` for hourly measurements?",
          "A) Errors out",
          "B) Reduces query speed",
          "C) Wastes storage buckets — match granularity to inter-arrival time (*)",
          "D) Doesn't allow inserts",
